  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The oxides which can react with both i.e acids and bases are called amphoteric oxides.<br />Oxides of vanadium <math> <mrow> <mfenced> <mtext>V</mtext> </mfenced></mrow> </math> and chromium <math> <mrow> <mfenced> <mrow> <mtext>Cr</mtext></mrow> </mfenced><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext></mrow> </math> show amphoteric nature in their oxides.<br />Hence <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>V</mtext> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mtext>5</mtext> </msub> <mtext>,</mtext><mtext> </mtext><msub> <mrow> <mtext>Cr</mtext></mrow> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math> is the correct option.",
